// A floating literal that keeps nothing of what was written is refused.
//
// std::stod throws on every value the C library flags as out of range, which
// includes subnormals, and the exception reached the user as a bare
// "Error: stod" -- no file, no line, and wrong besides, because 1e-308 is a
// value a double holds. Subnormals are accepted now
// (tests/floating-point-edges.abs); only a literal that overflows to infinity
// or underflows all the way to zero is refused, and it is refused where it is
// written.
//
// Compiled for the diagnostics, so the file never runs.

int32 main() {
    double tooLarge = 1e400;
    double tooSmall = 1e-400;
    return (tooLarge + tooSmall) as int32;
}
